  "tagline": "PostgreSQL fork that JIT-compiled OLAP queries with LLVM; superseded by Vitesse Data's Deepgreen DB.",
  "description": "Vitesse DB was a PostgreSQL-based analytical database from Vitesse Data, a Bay Area startup. Launched in 2014 on PostgreSQL 9.3.5 with binary compatibility, it compiled queries into native x86 code with LLVM, parsed CSV with SSE instructions and added a compressed column store, claiming large speedups on TPC-H style aggregates over stock PostgreSQL. A Vitesse X variant followed. The company later shifted to Deepgreen DB, its Greenplum-based MPP warehouse, and Vitesse DB disappeared from its product pages; by 2024 the site listed only Deepgreen, open-source Greenplum and Apache Geode support. Query JIT later became a standard PostgreSQL feature.",
